WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:07.430
So the big news that broke late Friday is
that indeed, Twitter has banned Donald Trump

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.980
permanently from its platform.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.769
We're going to go through the decision that
Twitter made and then talk about the implications.

00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:18.970
Twitter putting out a statement saying after
close review of recent tweets from the Trump

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:24.190
account and the context around them, specifically
how they're being received and interpreted

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:30.260
on and off Twitter, we have permanently suspended
the account due to the risk of further incitement

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.300
of violence in the context of horrific events
this week.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.210
We made it clear on Wednesday that additional
violations of the Twitter rules would potentially

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.790
result in this very course of action.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.850
Our public interest framework exists to enable
the public to hear from elected officials

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.000
and world leaders directly.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.829
It is built on a principle that the people
have a right to hold power to the account

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:52.690
to account in the open.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.450
However, we made it clear going back years
that these accounts are not above our rules

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.559
entirely and cannot use Twitter to incite
violence.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:04.530
Among other things, we will continue to be
transparent around our policies and their

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.530
enforcement.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:10.150
Now, reportedly when this happened, the word
being used is ballistic.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:14.280
Trump went ballistic at the White House when
he was banned from Twitter.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.880
A senior administration said that when Twitter
permanently took down Trump's account, Trump

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:23.270
was scrambling, trying to figure out what
to do.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.400
Initially, Trump started tweeting through
the official Perdis account.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.770
Now, the Perdis account is an account that
is in the hands of whoever is president.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.689
So it's not Trump's account.

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:37.220
It's Trump has access to it while being president
that has been shut down.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:43.850
Trump then tried tweeting through one of his
aides or staffers that was shut down.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:49.940
And the president reportedly running around
the White House going absolutely crazy.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:55.020
The White House then put out a statement saying
Trump is negotiating with other sites and

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:59.930
looking at building his own platform and blah,
blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:04.420
So there's a there's a number of different
important things we have to talk about here.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:12.260
First of all, there's lots of really bad arguments
being made by people on the right and people

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:17.861
on the left, including that Twitter shouldn't
be allowed to do this either because they

00:02:17.861 --> 00:02:23.720
are silencing only right wing voices, which
is untrue, or because Trump is president of

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.260
the United States.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:31.550
The guidelines are already a lower bar for
world leaders, Twitter has said, and it was

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.720
even implicit in the statement they put out.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:40.410
Twitter has said that when one is a world
leader, they air on the side of not taking

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:45.140
content down and not banning because they've
determined, and I agree with their determination

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.379
that it is important for us to know what world
leaders are saying.

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:54.790
However, we would expect our elected officials
to be held to a higher standard than the average

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.890
Twitter user with two followers sending me
hate tweets.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:58.890
Right.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:03.090
Like in other words, it's counterintuitive
that world leaders, some of the most powerful

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:08.250
people in the world, get held to an even lower
standard merely because they are world leaders.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.370
That's been the case all along.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:14.319
Twitter is a business that is allowed to have
terms of service and they're allowed to enforce

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:15.319
it.

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:20.450
But consider the greater hypocrisy that many
on the right are now essentially arguing Americans

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:27.310
have an inalienable right to be able to tweet
any limitation on their ability to tweet is

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.690
unconstitutional.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.690
It's a violation of rights granted by God.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:32.980
The Constitution, who knows?

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:36.010
And by the way, there's no right to health
care.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:39.580
Health care is a product that should be bought
and sold on the free market if you can afford

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:40.580
it.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:44.830
But you cannot be restricted in your ability
to tweet.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:46.100
Give me a break, guys.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.720
These people have been pathetic for a very
long time.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:54.170
Don Jr. then coming out and saying, whoa,
we have to do something about the market monopoly

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.190
power of Twitter.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.930
Where are we on antitrust?

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.900
Well, look at your dad.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:04.150
I have been out there for years saying we
are not and we've done.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:08.220
Multiple interviews, we are not dealing seriously.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:14.980
With the antitrust law that we have and we
have not enforced it, I've been talking about

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:20.259
that for years, but all of a sudden, the day
Trump's banned from Twitter, Don Jr. cares

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.489
about monopoly power.

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:23.229
Give me a break, guys.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:29.050
So the truth is, Trump's account should have
been removed long ago.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:32.900
There should be a higher standard on elected
officials, not a lower standard.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:36.099
And Trump got away with this long.

00:04:36.099 --> 00:04:38.129
But now there is sort of this deluge.

00:04:38.129 --> 00:04:42.340
There's for lack of a better term, these massive
dumps of bans and suspensions that are coming

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.970
now since the riotous insurrection.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:52.610
Now a cautionary message, despite my belief
that this is the right thing to do based on

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:58.090
Trump's use of Twitter and incitement to violence
and defense of the rioters, despite the fact

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:04.860
that we're saying it was correct to ban Trump
12 days before he leaves office forever.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:09.069
This is a sign of how much we've failed as
a country over the last four years to control

00:05:09.069 --> 00:05:12.319
Donald Trump and to hold accountable the people
who defended him.

00:05:12.319 --> 00:05:14.330
The rats leaving the sinking ship.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:20.419
Now, Betsy Davos, William Barr, Republican
Senator Pat Toomey, who now says Trump should

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.419
go.

00:05:21.419 --> 00:05:23.180
Chris Christie, who now says Trump should
be impeached.

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:24.469
They are right.

00:05:24.469 --> 00:05:25.509
Yes, sure.

00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:30.430
But we're 12, 11, 10 now, nine days out as
they are doing these things.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.009
They do not deserve to have their images rehabilitated.

00:05:34.009 --> 00:05:36.430
And we're going to talk about that after the
break.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:40.610
But we will have more coverage of the Trump
Twitter ban and social media implications

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:44.319
on our Instagram, where you can find us at
David Pakman show.

00:05:44.319 --> 00:06:55.969
And you can find me on Instagram as well at
David Pakman,

